<TextBox ID="37" X="500" Y="1460" Width="0">
<Text>
<![CDATA[Step Shutdown turns of both servos and jumps to the ladderfile.
The Transition waits for the timer in the ladderfile to time out then
directs program flow to loop back and turn the servo on and restart 
the sequence.]]>
</Text>
</TextBox>
<TextBox ID="38" X="640" Y="360" Width="0">
<Text>
<![CDATA[This program demonstrates how Sequential Function Chart programs work.
Rectangular blocks represent steps. Below each Step is a Transition. In order
for the program to progress to the next Step the Transition must be true.
The program below steps through:
Turning the servos on, monitoring inputs 1 &2 and changing the gear ratio up or
down based on the input status.  If Input 0 is enabled the program jumps to a 
subroutine waits 2 secs then restarts at ServosOn.]]>
</Text>
</TextBox>
<TextBox ID="39" X="640" Y="980" Width="0">
<Text>
<![CDATA[Monitors the status of inputs 1, 2 and 0 based on
which one is enabled the program changes the gear
ratio or shuts down and jumps to a subroutine]]>
</Text>
</TextBox>
</SFCContent>
</Routine>
